Um dos melhores jogos de rpg maker que já joguei.
Pontos positivos:
- Boa jogabilidade;
- Enredo interessante;
- Gráficos bacanas;
- Trilha sonora muito bem feita;
- Ampla diversidade de skills, buffs e magias (bem como suas combinações).
O único ponto negativo é que você joga majoritariamente com classes mágicas, exceto pelo Garic, que é arqueiro. Deveriam botar umas classes diferentes.
Recomendo fortemente aos que gostam do gênero e do estilo.
9,5/10.

This game is bad, not terribad but close.
First all the tongue in cheek humor about american "manifest destiny through war" may be fun for US citizens but i'm not american so it's lost on me.
The gameplay is SLOOOOOOOOOW and boring as it gets:
-the main move speed is walking, if you press a key you start running, no need for that simply remove the walking speed altogether and have running as main speed, one freed key for other actions, here it's a design failure;
-no instant-move like a dash or a roll, you can go prone to clear some effects on you (like fire) but you don't move while doing so and it's slow too;
-oh, if some enemies can hard crowd control you unto death they will, perma-cc on the player is a terrible game mechanism, perma-cc as a whole is always terrible because it is anti-action and so anti-game;
-when you start shooting you go back to walking speed, fair enough but then why does it take so much time to aim on top of that;
-the mag size of weapons is punny, adding sometime fatal reload time, in itself it's not bad but if it's like that for all weapons instead of being like that for some weapons then weapon gameplay diversity suffer.
Overall the gameplay is too slow for something as simple as a two-dimensions shooter nowadays.
The game as a whole feels well realized but lazily designed, the universe is bland and stereotyped, the gameplay is lukewarm at best, and the functionnalities are cumbersome (menus, droppables) and lacking (too few options to customize stuff).
Feels like a browser game, would make for a honorably forgettable f2p if it was free, but here as b2p (and dlc heavy) it's simply not worth the price at all to even consider.
I tried it on a free week-end for zero dosh.
Still want my money back.
